{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0438", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\cite{K-M}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{groupoids-section-introduction}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:90a2bf064332bd4bb991170c6cc01e889d8061582038695a4323ae990fa0c667", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis chapter is devoted to generalities concerning groupoids in algebraic\nspaces. We recommend reading the beautiful paper <REF_0001> by Keel and Mori.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nA lot of what we say here is a repeat of what we said in the chapter\non groupoid schemes, see\nGroupoids, Section <REF_0002>.\nThe discussion of quotient stacks is new here.\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:04798fba4495829ed730f6d45be653218c961584ae117c008dd87e01d749aac8", "unit_id": "tag:0438:prose-0001"}
